==Russian==

===Etymology===
Adaptation of a Western language {{l|en|lesbian}} (itself eventually tracing back to Ancient Greek {{l|grc|Λέσβος|t=[[Lesbos]]}}, the native island of {{w|Sappho}}, a poetess associated with female homosexuality in the Western literary canon) with the Russian feminizing suffix {{l|ru|-ка}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|лесбия́нка}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-лесбиянка.oga}}

===Noun===
